      "description": "The the cross-border MV systems lines extend from neighboring countries into Liberia. It was derived from a Government of Norway, World Bank, USAID & JICA funded study and brochures provided by LEC in 2012 ( World Bank. Scope and Rough Cost Estimate for Recovering Pre-War T&D System Capacity. May 2012) These lines were digitized by Earth Institute, Columbia University staff in New York. The three cross border systems are identified by the biggest settlement served in each system as (i) Yekepa, Nimba County (ii) Zwedru, Grand Gedeh County and (iii) Harper, Maryland County, respectively, from North to South. This data is from Liberia Power Sector Capacity Building and Energy Master Planning Final Report, Phase 4:National Electrification Master Plan on page 14 figure 2.",
